diff --git a/docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst b/docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst
index cb9a0df..3e64607 100644
--- a/docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst
+++ b/docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst
@@ -145,3 +145,32 @@ worker's startup message from actual completed DMA, and record failure
 injection separately. These counters describe only the synthetic model.
 The bus5 counter record also exposes the synthetic PSC control/status bytes,
 so integration evidence can establish CE-bit readback after a guest write.
+
+Opt-in inherited-display laboratory
+-----------------------------------
+
+``-M mt6762,lab-i2c=on,lab-display=on,lab-display-fb=0x41000000`` adds
+synthetic SPM, MMSYS, OVL0, RDMA0, DSI0 and DISP_PWM0 register fixtures. The
+explicit framebuffer must occupy a 16KiB-aligned 0x144000-byte guest RAM
+range entirely below 4GiB. Its pixels remain ordinary RAM; no scanout fetch,
+DSI packet, panel, backlight physics or IOMMU is emulated. ``lab-display``
+and its framebuffer address are immutable after machine initialization.
+
+Fixed readbacks describe one BGRA8888 OVL0 layer at 384x854, stride1536,
+RDMA direct-link, three DSI lanes and the recovered panel timing constants.
+Only PWM writes are accepted: the bounded duty latches on an ordered commit
+1-to-0 transition. PWM starts enabled at duty512, period1023, divider3. The
+shared TOPCKGEN fixture exposes PWM parent3 and an open gate only when this
+fixture is enabled. Other pipeline writes are rejected and counted.
+
+Dynamic ``lab-display-fault`` values ``none``, ``pwm-drop``, ``power-off`` and
+``scanout-mismatch`` exercise write/readback and inherited-handoff rejection.
+Read-only ``lab-display-state`` returns synthetic register-access counters,
+commit count and applied PWM level. Those counters can prove guest driver
+activity but cannot prove physical brightness or display operation.
+
+Run ``python3 tests/mt6762/test_lab_display.py --qemu build/qemu-system-aarch64
+--dtb /path/to/boot.bin.dtb`` for bounds, default absence, commit ordering,
+readback faults and rejected pipeline-write tests. Native XNU integration
+uses the separately packaged ``prepare.py --native-lab-display`` option;
+its assertions must never be copied into a real phone's loader handoff.
